  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "While scouting toward Bai Gu mountain, Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing find a rotting swamp southwest of a lava crocodile valley. From frogs screeching at the swamp center, Fang Yuan names the swamp’s lord as Poison Swallowing Toad.",
        "chapters": [
          207
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_bai_gu_mountain",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_bai_ning_bing"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The southwest swamp is a poison habitat of snakes, bees, and large black spiders. Entering the deep swamp to lure the toad out is harder than its poor speed alone would suggest, and the two travelers lack any healing Gu of their own, so a poisonous bite would be serious trouble. They do not capture it.",
        "chapters": [
          207
        ],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rotting-swamp-and-the-pheasant-night",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "During the night when a Xuan Yuan Divine Pheasant wrecks the valley and surrounding territories, Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing hear the poison swallowing toad’s screech among the other beasts’ cries. After the pheasant leaves, the swamp is ravaged and its forces are in chaos; the cited chapters do not say whether the toad survives, dies, or flees, and no later cited chapter names a capture or owner.",
        "chapters": [
          208
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rotting-swamp-and-the-pheasant-night",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
